==Old English==

===Etymology===
From {{proto|Germanic|swait-|lang=ang}}, from {{proto|Indo-European|swoid-|lang=ang}}. Cognate with Old Saxon {{term|swet|swêt|lang=osx}} Old High German {{term|sweiz|lang=goh}}, Old Norse {{term|sveiti||sweat, blood|lang=non}}. The Indo-European root also gave Latin {{term|sudor|lang=la}}, Sanskrit {{term|स्वेद|tr=sveda|lang=sa}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/swaːt/|lang=ang}}

===Noun===
{{ang-noun|g=m|head=swāt}}

# [[blood]]

